# 🚀 AI DevOps Assistant - Полная Инструкция

## Front door (mandatory)

**Workflow / gates:** Cursor command `/opsx-devops`  
**This file:** domain knowledge only (namespaces, monitoring, CSI policy, links).  
**Durable ops memory:** `.cursor/devops/OPS_STATE.md` + `LAST.json` (past actions / current release posture).  
**DB migrate procedure:** `DEVOPS_DB_MIGRATIONS.md` (CONTROL→Migrate→CAS).  
Do **not** treat attaching this rule alone as license for cluster writes.

| Mode | How | Mutates cluster? |
|------|-----|------------------|
| Investigate (default) | `/opsx-devops` or `/opsx-devops INVESTIGATE …` | No — read-only kubectl + repo reads |
| Plan write | `/opsx-devops PLAN_WRITE …` | No — plan + optional `--dry-run=client` |
| Apply write | `/opsx-devops GO …` with scoped plan | Yes — allowlisted ops only |
| Safe prod release | `/opsx-devops PLAN_WRITE\|GO intent=safe_prod_release …` | Yes — Job path + CAS only after GO |

Hard forbids (all modes; details in `/opsx-devops` + `local-production-entrypoints.mdc` / `debug-runtime.mdc`):

- `k8s/**csi**` apply/edit in provider cluster
- `kubectl port-forward` / cluster Redis tunnel for local debug
- printing Secret `data` values
- product `app/**` bugfixes (→ `/opsx-fix-bug`)
- laptop/`alembic upgrade` on prod; bare `kubectl set image` without CAS test+replace

Acknowledgement is not write approval. Cluster mutations require exact `GO` on `/opsx-devops`.  
`/opsx-devops` **must** read OPS_STATE at start and continue from it (not from empty chat).

